      en: "The mangrove ecosystem of the Gulf of Fonseca is a shared natural treasure of El Salvador, Honduras, and Nicaragua, possessing extraordinary ecological importance. This massive wetland serves as a natural filter and protective barrier for the coastline while providing a nursery for countless marine species. Along winding channels, red, black, and white mangrove trees form an impenetrable wall where herons, pelicans, and frigatebirds nest in large numbers. Visitors can tour the waterways by motorboat, observing the daily lives of fishers and wild animals. The tranquility of the gulf and the pristine nature radiate a special atmosphere. Geography K8"
